WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.560
Detection ideas can come from threat intelligence, incident lessons, threat hunting,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.055
red team exercises, vulnerability disclosures, business risks, compliance requirements,

00:00:09.055 --> 00:00:10.000
and analyst feedback.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.945
Not every idea deserves immediate development.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:16.690
Teams should prioritize based on relevance, expected value, available telemetry, impact,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.944
likelihood, and operational capacity.

00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:23.000
Prioritization prevents the detection backlog from becoming a random pile of requests.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.700
It helps teams focus on detections that are feasible, useful,

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.000
and connected to meaningful defensive outcomes.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
A good intake process also captures context.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The team should know who requested the detection, what behavior matters,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.960
what data may be needed, and how success will be recognized.
